{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466378",
      "title": "Multiple Interceptors",
      "lectureOrder": 600,
      "videoOrder": 553,
      "sourceHash": "c9ba8f959b8e6a5d5ae1199cbfc1647a0b363c6143b9baaf87ac0adf06bda664",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.19,
          "end": 4.8,
          "en": "Teacher: Now to finish up this topic on interceptors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.8,
          "end": 7.77,
          "en": "and by the way, we'll see interceptors again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.77,
          "end": 10.14,
          "en": "in the authentication section of this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.14,
          "end": 13.74,
          "en": "But to wrap it up for now, let's add a second interceptor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.74,
          "end": 15.15,
          "en": "Because you're not limited to one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.15,
          "end": 17.34,
          "en": "you can add as many as you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.34,
          "end": 20.07,
          "en": "I'll name this one logging interceptor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.07,
          "end": 22.303,
          "en": "because I only want to do some logging here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.303,
          "end": 24.09,
          "en": "and therefore the file name is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.09,
          "end": 28.141,
          "en": "logging-interceptor.service.ts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.141,
          "end": 31.17,
          "en": "And there we now will create a new interceptor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.17,
          "end": 32.49,
          "en": "Feel free to pause the video",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.49,
          "end": 34.84,
          "en": "at this point and try it on your own of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.32,
          "end": 38.592,
          "en": "You do create it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.592,
          "end": 42.12,
          "en": "by exporting a class which you should name appropriately",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.12,
          "end": 46.81,
          "en": "like logging interceptor service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.248,
          "end": 53.248,
          "en": "This has to implement the HTP interceptor interface",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.52,
          "end": 57.21,
          "en": "which you import from at Angular Common http.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.21,
          "end": 60.27,
          "en": "This forces you to add a INTERSET method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.27,
          "end": 62.07,
          "en": "which then in turn gets a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.07,
          "end": 63.905,
          "en": "which is of type HTP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.905,
          "end": 68.67,
          "en": "and which gets this next object function thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.67,
          "end": 70.92,
          "en": "which is a type HDP handler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.92,
          "end": 75.27,
          "en": "And there you should return next handle as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.27,
          "end": 77.76,
          "en": "And since HDP request is generic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.76,
          "end": 80.03999999999999,
          "en": "you should also add angle brackets there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.03999999999999,
          "end": 82.92,
          "en": "and define the type of data it will eventually wrap.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.92,
          "end": 86.43,
          "en": "Now to next handle, you also have to pass your request in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.43,
          "end": 87.99,
          "en": "This is a basic interceptor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.99,
          "end": 90.15,
          "en": "but of course it's not doing any logging",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.15,
          "end": 92.82,
          "en": "which it should if we have a look at the name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.82,
          "end": 94.77000000000001,
          "en": "So here I will now do some logging",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.77000000000001,
          "end": 97.05,
          "en": "and of course log whatever you want here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.05,
          "end": 102.05,
          "en": "So here I'll just log outgoing request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.19,
          "end": 107.58,
          "en": "and maybe also the URL though you could",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.58,
          "end": 110.22,
          "en": "of course also log the headers or whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.22,
          "end": 115.22,
          "en": "And on the response I will now again pipe the tap operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.22999999999999,
          "end": 116.13,
          "en": "which is imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.13,
          "end": 120.003,
          "en": "from RXJS/operators where I got the event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.78,
          "end": 126.39,
          "en": "And here we could now log all events again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.39,
          "end": 128.64,
          "en": "but I only care about the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.64,
          "end": 133.64,
          "en": "So I'll compare the event type to HDP event type response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.37,
          "end": 139.12,
          "en": "And in there we can console log incoming response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.06,
          "end": 143.49,
          "en": "and also console log event body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 143.49,
          "end": 145.98,
          "en": "So response body if you want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 145.98,
          "end": 148.56,
          "en": "Now it's a very simple logging interceptor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 148.56,
          "end": 149.7,
          "en": "in the off interceptor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.7,
          "end": 153.42000000000002,
          "en": "I'll dare get rid of that extra logging I'm doing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 153.42000000000002,
          "end": 155.73,
          "en": "So I'll get rid of that pipe method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.73,
          "end": 157.77,
          "en": "and just return the modified request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.77,
          "end": 161.059,
          "en": "I'll also not log these two statements here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 161.059,
          "end": 164.25,
          "en": "so that I have a leaner interceptor here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 164.25,
          "end": 167.67000000000002,
          "en": "So this interceptor is now only attaching the off header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 167.67000000000002,
          "end": 170.67000000000002,
          "en": "and the off interceptor is responsible for logging.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 170.67000000000002,
          "end": 172.74,
          "en": "Now we just need to add them both.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 172.74,
          "end": 175.29,
          "en": "And now here comes something super important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 175.29,
          "end": 178.53,
          "en": "The order in which you provide them matters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 178.53,
          "end": 181.75,
          "en": "because that will be the order in which they are executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 181.75,
          "end": 183.9,
          "en": "So in the app module here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 183.9,
          "end": 186.33,
          "en": "of course we provide the outer interceptor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 186.33,
          "end": 187.44,
          "en": "the logging interceptor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 187.44,
          "end": 191.13,
          "en": "by simply repeating this object in that provider's array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 191.13,
          "end": 195.06,
          "en": "And here you now point at that logging intercepting service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 195.06,
          "end": 196.471,
          "en": "which you have to import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 196.471,
          "end": 200.22,
          "en": "But now this off interceptor will run first",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 200.22,
          "end": 202.95,
          "en": "and thereafter comes to logging interceptor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 202.95,
          "end": 205.751,
          "en": "Now often the order might not matter, but if it does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 205.751,
          "end": 207.81,
          "en": "be aware of that order",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 207.81,
          "end": 210.32999999999998,
          "en": "and order your interceptors accordingly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 210.32999999999998,
          "end": 214.17000000000002,
          "en": "so that the order in which they execute fits your use case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 214.17000000000002,
          "end": 216.69,
          "en": "and whatever you're doing in your interceptors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 216.69,
          "end": 218.61,
          "en": "And to prove that order thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 218.61,
          "end": 220.14,
          "en": "In the logging interceptor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 220.14,
          "end": 223.8,
          "en": "I'll actually also console log the request headers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 223.8,
          "end": 227.79,
          "en": "'cause there since the logging interceptor comes second,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 227.79,
          "end": 231.838,
          "en": "we should see that custom key, this off key being added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 231.838,
          "end": 234.039,
          "en": "So now if that, if we save that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 234.039,
          "end": 237.901,
          "en": "Let me clear the console and fetch again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 237.901,
          "end": 242.28,
          "en": "We see outgoing requests and URL, we see the headers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 242.28,
          "end": 245.22,
          "en": "And in there indeed we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 245.22,
          "end": 249.25,
          "en": "that off thing with the value of x y set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 249.25,
          "end": 253.175,
          "en": "And we have incoming response and we see the response body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 253.175,
          "end": 256.29,
          "en": "And now to really prove that order thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 256.29,
          "end": 259.26,
          "en": "remember that here we see off x y set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 259.26,
          "end": 262.65,
          "en": "Now I guess you can already imagine what will happen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 262.65,
          "end": 264.66,
          "en": "if I switch the order here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 264.66,
          "end": 267.661,
          "en": "and we log first and thereafter we add the key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 267.661,
          "end": 271.031,
          "en": "Well, if we do that and I clear that and then I fetch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 271.031,
          "end": 274.95,
          "en": "then of course you see we still log the same as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 274.95,
          "end": 276.749,
          "en": "But if we inspect our headers here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 276.749,
          "end": 280.05,
          "en": "we only got that custom header, which we're not setting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 280.05,
          "end": 283.68,
          "en": "in an interceptor, we're missing the off header though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 283.68,
          "end": 285.54,
          "en": "So the order matters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 285.54,
          "end": 286.5,
          "en": "But other than that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 286.5,
          "end": 289.35,
          "en": "providing multiple interceptors is extremely simple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 289.35,
          "end": 290.183,
          "en": "as you can tell.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
